WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.749 --> 00:00:02.482
Everything's so tiny.

00:00:02.482 --> 00:00:06.315
(mysterious fast-paced music)

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.848
Today we're going to be taking

00:00:08.848 --> 00:00:11.085
a surgeon try out test from Japan.

00:00:11.085 --> 00:00:13.778
So I was actually was premed
when I was in college.

00:00:13.778 --> 00:00:16.245
I did not continue being premed

00:00:16.245 --> 00:00:18.314
because I wanted to make art.

00:00:18.314 --> 00:00:21.995
I was premed up until my
junior year of college.

00:00:21.995 --> 00:00:25.632
While I really enjoyed learning
about biology and science,

00:00:25.632 --> 00:00:26.824
and I still really love science.

00:00:26.824 --> 00:00:30.796
It just ultimately didn't seem
like the best choice for me.

00:00:30.796 --> 00:00:34.629
(mysterious fast-paced music)

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:43.968
It's like a Jason Bourne movie.

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:46.118
Oh my gosh, that's a tiny ass bird.

00:00:46.118 --> 00:00:48.430
This is stressful though,
I'm getting like sweaty

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:49.358
just watching this.

00:00:49.358 --> 00:00:51.419
I feel like it seems like defusing a bomb.

00:00:51.419 --> 00:00:52.527
That is insane.

00:00:52.527 --> 00:00:54.487
They're doing it with one grain of rice?

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.028
It's sushi for ants.

00:00:56.028 --> 00:00:57.076
Wait this is insane.

00:00:57.076 --> 00:00:58.137
I don't know if I want to do this.

00:00:58.137 --> 00:00:59.367
I don't know if I can do this.

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:02.117
(dramatic music)

00:01:07.796 --> 00:01:09.407
Okay, this won't be so bad.

00:01:09.407 --> 00:01:12.055
Wait, no, everything is
already going horribly wrong.

00:01:12.055 --> 00:01:14.365
This is comical, I don't
know why I'm doing this.

00:01:14.365 --> 00:01:15.415
I will say though,

00:01:15.415 --> 00:01:17.813
that if I get more than two of these done,

00:01:17.813 --> 00:01:22.276
I expect to automatically be
given a surgeon certification.

00:01:22.276 --> 00:01:24.927
I just want to get my
face really close to it

00:01:24.927 --> 00:01:28.516
and I feel like it'll make it
easier but it's not going to.

00:01:28.516 --> 00:01:31.594
I'm so sorry in advance to my family,

00:01:31.594 --> 00:01:33.185
my scholarship donors.

00:01:33.185 --> 00:01:35.093
I failed you all.

00:01:35.093 --> 00:01:37.295
Man, these creases are just so helpful.

00:01:37.295 --> 00:01:39.985
You don't even realize
why you're making them.

00:01:39.985 --> 00:01:42.236
Beautiful. Okay, so it is
more like a paper swan.

00:01:42.236 --> 00:01:43.069
Look at this.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:43.994
It's like the size,

00:01:43.994 --> 00:01:45.194
what is this the size of?

00:01:45.194 --> 00:01:47.476
It's like the size of my ear hole.

00:01:47.476 --> 00:01:49.455
I'm reevaluating so many life choices.

00:01:49.455 --> 00:01:50.783
I will not be making three of these

00:01:50.783 --> 00:01:51.847
but I maybe I can make two.

00:01:51.847 --> 00:01:54.095
Oh my god, I just realized
that I need to fold this again.

00:01:54.095 --> 00:01:55.104
Are you serious?

00:01:55.104 --> 00:01:56.886
I'm not sure if this really helps

00:01:56.886 --> 00:01:58.775
because what if you're a
surgeon who just happens

00:01:58.775 --> 00:02:03.273
to be really great at origami
but you suck at surgery.

00:02:03.273 --> 00:02:04.781
Just do it.

00:02:04.781 --> 00:02:06.697
Just fold the way that I want you to fold.

00:02:06.697 --> 00:02:08.699
Is that what being a parent feels like?

00:02:08.699 --> 00:02:10.819
You're just whispering
in your kid's ear like,

00:02:10.819 --> 00:02:11.960
be a doctor.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:14.200
I don't know if I buy this as a test.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.464
Manual dexterity measure, sure.

00:02:16.464 --> 00:02:19.909
Overall, surgery skill measure, mm.

00:02:19.909 --> 00:02:21.806
Oh my gosh, let's go.

00:02:21.806 --> 00:02:23.579
Wait no dang it, I'm missing a fold.

00:02:23.579 --> 00:02:26.329
(dramatic music)

00:02:27.515 --> 00:02:29.339
Look at those sitting next to each other.

00:02:29.339 --> 00:02:30.579
I'm still okay with it

00:02:30.579 --> 00:02:32.200
and I'm actually very happy with it.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.429
I think I did great.

00:02:33.429 --> 00:02:34.262
What do you think?

00:02:34.262 --> 00:02:36.379
Am I getting that surgical
residency or what?

00:02:36.379 --> 00:02:39.129
(dramatic music)

00:02:44.669 --> 00:02:46.859
I'm very confident in this.

00:02:46.859 --> 00:02:48.448
I think what I'm going to do

00:02:48.448 --> 00:02:50.029
is I'm going to make an assembly line.

00:02:50.029 --> 00:02:53.859
I'm going for the easiest
cut, if that makes sense.

00:02:53.859 --> 00:02:54.880
Like I'm going for the section

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:56.728
where I can already see it shaped

00:02:56.728 --> 00:03:00.936
or taking on the form of the larger model.

00:03:00.936 --> 00:03:02.288
- [Sydnee] Would it be
funny if I accidentally

00:03:02.288 --> 00:03:04.728
severed my finger with
this miniature knife?

00:03:04.728 --> 00:03:06.399
So what's frustrating me a little bit

00:03:06.399 --> 00:03:09.589
is that the texture of some
of these pieces of flesh

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:12.928
is more difficult to work with than others

00:03:12.928 --> 00:03:15.328
but again, much like the human body.

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:16.608
- [Syndee] I'm sure when
they actually do it though

00:03:16.608 --> 00:03:18.800
they probably have a specific
way they have to cut the fish

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:21.040
instead of just slicing a sad piece.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.759
Best believe I will be eating everything

00:03:23.759 --> 00:03:26.488
on this cutting board by the
time we are done here today.

00:03:26.488 --> 00:03:28.288
- [Sydnee] Okay, we're going
to cheat this a little bit

00:03:28.288 --> 00:03:31.059
and make it look nice from the top.

00:03:31.059 --> 00:03:32.948
(laughing)

00:03:32.948 --> 00:03:36.448
Moment of truth, this will
not be easy, my friends

00:03:36.448 --> 00:03:39.568
but this is what I went to
fake sushi surgery school for.

00:03:39.568 --> 00:03:41.848
I got a little bit cocky, you guys.

00:03:41.848 --> 00:03:44.614
I just decided that I was
going to make it perfect.

00:03:44.614 --> 00:03:47.364
(dramatic music)

00:03:59.219 --> 00:04:01.640
Isn't a surgeon just making
sure that your patient is alive?

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:03.229
It doesn't have to be pretty.

00:04:03.229 --> 00:04:04.499
I just want to take it home

00:04:04.499 --> 00:04:09.024
and feed them to tiny
imaginary mouse friend.

00:04:09.024 --> 00:04:10.762
I think I kinda crushed it.

00:04:10.762 --> 00:04:12.591
I feel like I'm 2/3 of a surgeon now.

00:04:12.591 --> 00:04:14.690
Definitely a lot better
than screwing around with

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:17.714
Lewis structures and the
Krebs cycle and stuff.

00:04:17.714 --> 00:04:21.922
If I had to deal with the
stress of I could kill someone

00:04:21.922 --> 00:04:24.372
literally every time I step into work,

00:04:24.372 --> 00:04:26.434
that just doesn't sound very fun to me.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:27.674
It makes me feel like for sure

00:04:27.674 --> 00:04:29.011
I could not be a surgeon though.

00:04:29.011 --> 00:04:31.491
Thank you to all the
surgeons and all the doctors

00:04:31.491 --> 00:04:36.002
who go through an incredible
amount of commitment

00:04:36.002 --> 00:04:39.002
to their education just
to help other people.

00:04:39.002 --> 00:04:40.252
Thank you, that's awesome.

00:04:40.252 --> 00:04:42.411
I think I won.

00:04:42.411 --> 00:04:44.914
I'm proud of what I did here today.

00:04:44.914 --> 00:04:46.401
This was so hard.

00:04:46.401 --> 00:04:48.984
(upbeat music)

